      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<div class=\"sbn-doc sbn-doc-foto\"><div class=\"sbn-foto-imagen\"><img class=\"sbn-doc-imagen\" src=\"modules/seattle-by-night/assets/handouts/AYU-06-IMG.webp\" alt=\"\"><p class=\"sbn-foto-descripcion\"><span class=\"sbn-acotacion\">[photo]</span> A pile of gray ash on wet concrete, next to the base of a red shipping container. On top of the ash, a black nylon jacket, intact. On the side of the container, at a man&#39;s chest height, three dents in a vertical line, one below the other. A yellow scale ruler on the ground. A numbered marker: 3.</p></div>\n<p class=\"sbn-foto-pie\">PORT OF SEATTLE · PORT POLICE · CASE 26-3307 · PHOTO 3 OF 14 · 11/13/2026 · 5:06 AM</p>\n<aside class=\"sbn-manuscrito sbn-manuscrito-lapiz\"><p><span class=\"sbn-acotacion\">[On the back of the photo, in pencil:]</span> <em>What burns without burning the jacket?</em></p></aside>\n</div>"
